THE CELL A HUMAN WROTE
----------------------
# the distribution is the whole point of this board
hist = df.hist( bins = 30 )   # 30 is deliberate, do not tidy this
get(source) -> inlets ['df'], outlets ['hist']

GESTURE 1 · REBIND — drag the `norm` cable onto the `df` inlet
--------------------------------------------------------------
# the distribution is the whole point of this board
hist = norm.hist( bins = 30 )   # 30 is deliberate, do not tidy this
get(put(source, norm)) -> inlets ['norm']
  round-trip law, get(put(w)) == w : True
  comment above survived           : True
  trailing comment survived        : True
  the spacing nobody would choose  : True
  the outlet was NOT touched       : True

THE UNDOABILITY TEST (Lechtenboerger, PODS 2003)
------------------------------------------------
  drag `df` back onto the inlet -> byte-identical to the original? True
  => REBIND is undoable from inside the view, so it is a legal silent drag.

GESTURE 2 · RENAME a port
-------------------------
  producer : norm = df / df.max()   # normalised, see the memo
  rebind('norm'->'scaled') on the producer leaves the BINDING alone:
             norm = df / df.max()   # normalised, see the memo
  => a rename is two edits, not one: rebind every consumer, then re-bind the
     producer. marimo's single-definition rule is what makes it exact — one
     producer, N consumers, all statically known, so it is a correct global
     refactor rather than a search-and-replace.

GESTURE 3 · CUT — deleting a cable is not an edit at all
--------------------------------------------------------
  hist = df.hist(bins=30)    remove the `df` reference and you are left with
  hist = .hist(bins=30)      which is not Python. There is no name to put there.
  Undoable from inside the view? NO — the undo needs the expression you deleted,
  and the wire never carried it.
  Same for CONNECT into a block that references nothing: there is no inlet to
  land on, so the tool must ask WHERE, and a drag cannot ask.

THE BAND, STATED ONCE
---------------------
  legal as a silent drag : REBIND an existing inlet · RENAME a port
  named command, preview : CONNECT a new reference · CUT · anything abstracting
  never under a drag     : an LLM. Too slow, nondeterministic and untestable at
                           interaction speed; it proposes a diff, it is not the
                           edit engine. (Round Tripping note, Rule 6.)
